{
  "name": "berm/pocket/generated-identity",
  "version": 2,
  "frozen": true,
  "supersedes": "version 1, which exposed a separate spendingKeyHex",
  "note": "PATH A ONLY \u2014 freshly generated identities. The secret is normalised for BIP-340 parity BEFORE it is ever treated as the user's key, so the exported secret DIRECTLY controls the EVM address with no later transformation. Version 1 carried a distinct spendingKeyHex; a user who exported the nsec and imported it into a wallet would have landed on a different address than the one displayed. That is a trap and it is removed rather than documented.",
  "invariants": [
    "secretKeyHex always has EVEN-y \u2014 assert it, do not assume it",
    "nsec and evmAddress are controlled by the SAME exported secret",
    "npub is unchanged by negation: x-only is the x coordinate, which negation preserves",
    "no spendingKeyHex field exists, and none should be reintroduced"
  ],
  "derivation": [
    "d = raw if y(raw*G) even else n - raw   <-- AT GENERATION",
    "xonly = x(d*G)",
    "npub = bech32('npub', xonly)",
    "nsec = bech32('nsec', d)",
    "evmAddress = keccak256(x || y)[12:] of d*G, EIP-55 checksummed"
  ],
